==Danish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|da|/svaːˀr/|[ˈsʋ̥ɑˀ]}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|da|non|svar||answer, reply}}, either derived from the verb {{m|non|svara}} or inherited from {{inh|da|gem-pro|*swarō||solemn statement}}, cognate with {{cog|en|swear}}. Compare also the compound {{m|gem-pro|*andaswarō||reply}} in {{cog|en|answer}} and {{cog|da|ansvar||responsibility}}.

====Noun====
{{da-noun|et}}

# [[answer]] {{q|response}}
# [[reply]]
# [[response]]
# [[retort]], [[repartee]]

=====Inflection=====
{{da-decl|et}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|da|non|svárr}}, from {{inh|da|gem-pro|*swēraz}}, cognate with {{cog|sv|svår}}, {{cog|de|schwer}}, {{cog|nl|zwaar}}. {{doublet|da|svær}}. The Danish form with ''a'' is influenced by {{cog|gml|swār}}.

